a malloc-free reverse-mode autograd engine in c,
built to train karpathy's microGPT as fast as possible.


all memory is static, handed out by a port of zig's FixedBufferAllocator.

1000 training steps take 0.107s on one core.


usage:

    $ make parity

    trained 1000 steps in 0.107s
    passed parity check (max abs diff 5.7e-15)
    inference (random sampled name): kaonle


see also:

- discussion on hackernews: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46285424
- counterpart in lean: https://github.com/sueszli/autograd.lean
- original microgpt implementation: https://karpathy.github.io/2026/02/12/microgpt/
- tigerstyle: https://github.com/tigerbeetle/tigerbeetle/blob/main/docs/TIGER_STYLE.md
- zig's FixedBufferAllocator: https://ziglang.org/documentation/master/std/#std.heap.FixedBufferAllocator
